mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>Histology and Embryology are two interrelated yet independent disciplines. Through theoretical and practical instruction, the course aims to equip students with knowledge of the microscopic and ultrastructural features of various cells, tissues, and major organs, as well as their correlation with corresponding functions. Additionally, students will master the early development of human embryos and the developmental patterns of principal organs, thereby laying a solid foundation for subsequent studies in other basic medical and clinical medicine courses.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
